{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/apple/check-build-version.sh","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:43:36.758248Z","id":"a820bbfed034f299089e0d3c7d5c12aad617a19bb37e35d465a92589d6b69d5f","body":{"detail":"Rust 1.94's prebuilt standard library carries its own minimum: in libclax_ios.a built by //crates/clax-ios:clax_ios_builds at 02fd07054, 384 of 2769 members (std, core's dependencies, compiler_builtins, unwind) are minos 14.0 on the simulator and LC_VERSION_MIN_IPHONEOS 10.0 on a device; the other 2385, every crate Bazel compiles and the C of ring and SQLite, are 17.0 (bazel-out/darwin_arm64-fastbuild/bin/crates/clax-ios/clax_ios_builds/*.build_version). An exact match would need the standard library rebuilt for 17.0 (-Zbuild-std, nightly only). An older object links without a warning; only a newer one makes ld warn.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":59},"end":{"line":70},"content_hash":"5e43519d5559c49232a3beecd4bbafe8704b779b4cfa59c2efce90541836bf5c"},"summary":"Require minos to equal --ios_minimum_os on every object, rather than be no newer","tags":["revisit:build-std is stable, or Rust's iOS std targets 17.0 or later","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/apple/ios_rust.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T05:43:36.758309Z","id":"39cbbcb160719cce17ec2c9c39f15538cc3aae679281ef07a84be0f81e284591","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //crates/clax-ios:clax_ios_static --platforms=@apple_support//platforms:ios_sim_arm64 compiles every Rust crate at minos 14.0 (rustc's default for aarch64-apple-ios-sim), because .bazelrc's --ios_minimum_os reaches rustc only through _deployment_target in ios_opt_library's and ios_builds' transitions. The app links :clax_ios_c, which goes through :clax_ios_opt, so it is not affected; an older Rust object is also accepted by check-build-version.sh. Setting --@rules_rust//rust/settings:extra_rustc_env globally in .bazelrc would cover it, at the cost of changing the action key of every Rust action on every platform.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"51ec541e648b35acdd254b0d56824d10448e5a9d1284c1a3c3417ec426e7cadd"},"summary":"Only the two transitions here give rustc IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET: :clax_ios_static built directly for an iOS platform has Rust objects at rustc's default minimum","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/apple/signing.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:29:36.457339Z","id":"4441051afde5b84891e56e7378d659da63d2103a2306d14021f12377cfff9334","body":{"detail":"ctx.watch and ctx.watch_tree catch a file added, removed, changed or chmodded, but not a mode change of the directory itself (bazel/apple/signing-test.sh step 4 shows it: after chmod 755 the build still passes until `bazelisk fetch --force --repo=@clax_apple_signing`). So a directory loosened after a passing evaluation keeps building until the next server start (.bazelrc: --max_idle_secs=900) or refetch, and one tightened after a refusal keeps refusing until the fetch the message names. Accepted: the check is hygiene for files that stay on this Mac, and every file's own mode is checked on every change.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":122},"end":{"line":135},"content_hash":"9448bccd28cfeb9cd02010a038a8c75de474f0303127dc68219e4820dfc33abe"},"summary":"A chmod of the signing directory alone is not seen until @clax_apple_signing is fetched again","tags":["signing","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/apple/ios_rust.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T22:27:54.112490Z","id":"9b06686b7bf8bde9358e405dca1c8715d2d903104fb915b1a8c5bc0037124e04","body":{"detail":"bazelisk build //crates/clax-ios:clax_ios_static --platforms=@apple_support//platforms:ios_sim_arm64 compiled every Rust crate at minos 14.0 (rustc's default for aarch64-apple-ios-sim), because .bazelrc's --ios_minimum_os reaches rustc only through _deployment_target in ios_opt_library's and ios_builds' transitions. crates/clax-ios is deleted; clax-embed's static library goes through the same rules (crates/clax-embed/BUILD.bazel: clax_embed_ios_opt, clax_embed_ios_builds), so the same holds for :clax_embed_static built directly (not measured for it). The app links :clax_embed_ios_c, which goes through :clax_embed_ios_opt, so it is not affected; an older Rust object is also accepted by check-build-version.sh. Setting --@rules_rust//rust/settings:extra_rustc_env globally in .bazelrc would cover it, at the cost of changing the action key of every Rust action on every platform.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"51ec541e648b35acdd254b0d56824d10448e5a9d1284c1a3c3417ec426e7cadd"},"summary":"Only the two transitions here give rustc IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET: //crates/clax-embed:clax_embed_static built directly for an iOS platform has Rust objects at rustc's default minimum","supersedes":"39cbbcb160719cce17ec2c9c39f15538cc3aae679281ef07a84be0f81e284591","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
